{"vid":"rCIs5x0SGTY","source":"rCIs5x0SGTY.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.1,"txt":"Hello and welcome to 6 Minute English from BBC Learning English."},{"t":4.3,"txt":"I'm Georgie."},{"t":5.2,"txt":"And I'm Neil."},{"t":6.3,"txt":"Don't forget you can find vocabulary, definitions"},{"t":9.2,"txt":"and a worksheet for free on our website, bbclearningenglish.com."},{"t":14.9,"txt":"So Neil, today we're talking about rejection."},{"t":18.9,"txt":"So, rejection means saying no to someone"},{"t":21.6,"txt":"or refusing to accept their idea or suggestion."},{"t":25.7,"txt":"Neil, how do you feel about rejection?"},{"t":28.2,"txt":"Well, nobody likes rejection."},{"t":31.8,"txt":"But I think as you get older, you get used to it."},{"t":35.7,"txt":"And probably it's quite a good thing to experience rejection,"},{"t":40.5,"txt":"even if it doesn't feel nice."},{"t":42.7,"txt":"Yeah, I agree."},{"t":44,"txt":"We can't always get what we want, can we?"},{"t":45.9,"txt":"We can't, no."},{"t":47.1,"txt":"In this podcast,"},{"t":48.2,"txt":"we'll be learning about a new internet trend called rejection therapy"},{"t":52.7,"txt":"and how people are using it to help them to be more confident."},{"t":59.3,"txt":"OK. Let's start with our quiz question, Georgie."},{"t":62.3,"txt":"Lots of famous people"},{"t":64.1,"txt":"have faced rejection in their lives before they became successful,"},{"t":68.7,"txt":"but which of these things did not happen to the animator Walt Disney"},{"t":73.7,"txt":"before he became successful?"},{"t":75.7,"txt":"Was it: a) he lost his job as an artist, b) his first business ran out of money,"},{"t":82.7,"txt":"or c) his first full length film was a failure?"},{"t":86.7,"txt":"I've got no idea, but I'm going to go with a) he lost his job as an artist."},{"t":92.1,"txt":"OK. Well, we'll find out the answer at the end of the programme."},{"t":95.8,"txt":"OK Neil. So, most people don't like being rejected,"},{"t":99.6,"txt":"but one thing to try might be something called rejection therapy."},{"t":104.7,"txt":"It's a social media trend where people record themselves talking to strangers"},{"t":109.6,"txt":"and sometimes being rejected."},{"t":113.1,"txt":"OK. That sounds quite interesting,"},{"t":115.3,"txt":"but let's find out how it works in practice."},{"t":118.6,"txt":"Hannah Gelbart, host of the BBC World Service podcast"},{"t":122.5,"txt":"What in the World, had a go at the trend."},{"t":125.4,"txt":"Let's see how she got on."},{"t":128,"txt":"Hey, can I come sit down at your table?"},{"t":130.3,"txt":"Yeah."},{"t":130.9,"txt":"Hey, how's it going?"},{"t":132,"txt":"Good, thank you."},{"t":132.8,"txt":"How's your day gone?"},{"t":133.9,"txt":"Good afternoon. How are you doing?"},{"t":136.3,"txt":"Can I drive your cab?"},{"t":139.5,"txt":"Can I? Can I get behind the wheel?"},{"t":141.6,"txt":"Don't be silly...!"},{"t":143.1,"txt":"Coming somewhere else to try and face my fears..."},{"t":146.5,"txt":"maybe do a bit of shopping."},{"t":148.1,"txt":"I was wondering, can I have a nap in one of these beds?"},{"t":150.2,"txt":"Can I just try it out?"},{"t":151.4,"txt":"Wow – I didn't expect that one to be a yes!"},{"t":154,"txt":"Well, it seems like people were pretty nice to Hannah in those examples."},{"t":157.7,"txt":"Yes. And she talks with psychologist Claudia Hammond"},{"t":161.2,"txt":"about how she felt during the experiment."},{"t":163.8,"txt":"And actually walking up to the first person,"},{"t":166,"txt":"I felt my adrenaline really, really spiking."},{"t":168.6,"txt":"I'm not a socially anxious person."},{"t":170.1,"txt":"I think I'm really confident."},{"t":171.8,"txt":"But that first thing really scared me."},{"t":173.8,"txt":"And once I'd done one, the second one came easier"},{"t":176.5,"txt":"and the third one came even easier. And you know,"},{"t":178.4,"txt":"by the fourth time I didn't even mind it whether they said yes or no."},{"t":181.9,"txt":"Hannah says that when she walked up to the first stranger in the video,"},{"t":185.7,"txt":"she felt her adrenaline spiking."},{"t":188.4,"txt":"If something spikes, it increases sharply."},{"t":191.4,"txt":"Hannah is not generally a socially anxious person."},{"t":195,"txt":"Someone who is socially anxious is nervous or worried"},{"t":198.9,"txt":"about speaking to other people."},{"t":201,"txt":"Each time Hannah tried to speak to a new person, she says, it came easier."},{"t":206.3,"txt":"Come easier is an informal way to say something is easier to achieve."},{"t":211.2,"txt":"Now, this social media trend is called rejection therapy,"},{"t":215.5,"txt":"but it's not a proper form of therapy."},{"t":218.4,"txt":"It hasn't been tested."},{"t":220,"txt":"And there are some criticisms of the videos because they involve filming"},{"t":224,"txt":"your interactions with strangers, which people might not want."},{"t":228,"txt":"But people who post the videos say they boost their confidence."},{"t":232.5,"txt":"So, why do people want to ask for rejection?"},{"t":236.3,"txt":"Psychologist Claudia Hammond has some ideas, which she shared with Hannah"},{"t":240.9,"txt":"on the BBC World Service podcast What in the World."},{"t":244.7,"txt":"What we do know is that there is an increase in perfectionism."},{"t":248.3,"txt":"People are more worried now, younger people,"},{"t":250.4,"txt":"about how other people are judging them."},{"t":252,"txt":"And so, I wonder whether that might make people more shy of speaking to strangers –"},{"t":257.3,"txt":"worried that the people will, you know, not appraise them in a good way,"},{"t":261.6,"txt":"and so doing something like this to try to counter that might feel"},{"t":266.2,"txt":"like a positive step to people, that they're trying to do something."},{"t":269.1,"txt":"Also, they're fun to watch."},{"t":270.7,"txt":"Claudia says there's an increase in perfectionism among young people."},{"t":275.6,"txt":"Perfectionism is the feeling that everything you do needs to be perfect."},{"t":280.5,"txt":"Young people are also worried about how people will appraise them,"},{"t":284.7,"txt":"which means judge them."},{"t":287.3,"txt":"Deliberately looking for rejection"},{"t":288.8,"txt":"might be an extreme way to become more confident,"},{"t":292,"txt":"but it can lead to surprising discoveries."},{"t":295.3,"txt":"Yes, and Hannah found that most strangers she spoke to were friendly"},{"t":299.3,"txt":"and happy to help, so she didn't really experience rejection much at all."},{"t":303.9,"txt":"OK. Georgie, I think it's time now for the answer to my quiz question."},{"t":308.6,"txt":"I asked you which rejection Walt Disney didn't experience"},{"t":314.1,"txt":"before becoming successful?"},{"t":315.9,"txt":"Yes, and I went for a) I don't think he lost his job as an artist."},{"t":321.5,"txt":"Well, actually, the answer was c) his first full length film, Snow White"},{"t":326.5,"txt":"and the Seven Dwarfs, was not a failure."},{"t":328.9,"txt":"It was a huge success."},{"t":330.8,"txt":"Wow! That was his first film?"},{"t":332.8,"txt":"That's really impressive."},{"t":334,"txt":"It is."},{"t":334.9,"txt":"OK. Let's recap the vocabulary we learned in this programme,"},{"t":338.7,"txt":"starting with 'rejection', which means saying no"},{"t":342.3,"txt":"or refusing an idea or suggestion."},{"t":345.1,"txt":"The verb 'spike' means increase suddenly."},{"t":348.1,"txt":"Someone who is socially anxious is nervous or worried"},{"t":352.1,"txt":"about speaking to other people."},{"t":354.3,"txt":"If something comes easier, it's easier to achieve."},{"t":358,"txt":"'Perfectionism' is the feeling that everything you do needs to be perfect."},{"t":362.7,"txt":"And if you appraise someone, you judge them."},{"t":366.4,"txt":"Once again, our six minutes are up,"},{"t":368.4,"txt":"but you can test what you've learned with the free worksheet"},{"t":371.1,"txt":"on our website, bbclearningenglish.com."},{"t":375,"txt":"Thank you for joining us and goodbye."},{"t":376.7,"txt":"Goodbye."}],"words":[{"t":0.083,"w":"Hello"},{"t":0.083,"w":"and"},{"t":0.083,"w":"welcome"},{"t":0.083,"w":"to"},{"t":0.083,"w":"6"},{"t":0.083,"w":"Minute"},{"t":0.083,"w":"English"},{"t":0.083,"w":"from"},{"t":0.083,"w":"BBC"},{"t":0.083,"w":"Learning"},{"t":0.083,"w":"English."},{"t":4.338,"w":"I'm"},{"t":4.338,"w":"Georgie."},{"t":5.172,"w":"And"},{"t":5.172,"w":"I'm"},{"t":5.172,"w":"Neil."},{"t":6.34,"w":"Don't"},{"t":6.34,"w":"forget"},{"t":6.34,"w":"you"},{"t":6.34,"w":"can"},{"t":6.34,"w":"find"},{"t":6.34,"w":"vocabulary,"},{"t":6.34,"w":"definitions"},{"t":9.218,"w":"and"},{"t":9.218,"w":"a"},{"t":9.218,"w":"worksheet"},{"t":9.218,"w":"for"},{"t":9.218,"w":"free"},{"t":9.218,"w":"on"},{"t":9.218,"w":"our"},{"t":9.218,"w":"website,"},{"t":9.218,"w":"bbclearningenglish.com."},{"t":14.89,"w":"So"},{"t":14.89,"w":"Neil,"},{"t":14.89,"w":"today"},{"t":14.89,"w":"we're"},{"t":14.89,"w":"talking"},{"t":14.89,"w":"about"},{"t":14.89,"w":"rejection."},{"t":18.936,"w":"So,"},{"t":18.936,"w":"rejection"},{"t":18.936,"w":"means"},{"t":18.936,"w":"saying"},{"t":18.936,"w":"no"},{"t":18.936,"w":"to"},{"t":18.936,"w":"someone"},{"t":21.605,"w":"or"},{"t":21.605,"w":"refusing"},{"t":21.605,"w":"to"},{"t":21.605,"w":"accept"},{"t":21.605,"w":"their"},{"t":21.605,"w":"idea"},{"t":21.605,"w":"or"},{"t":21.605,"w":"suggestion."},{"t":25.734,"w":"Neil,"},{"t":25.734,"w":"how"},{"t":25.734,"w":"do"},{"t":25.734,"w":"you"},{"t":25.734,"w":"feel"},{"t":25.734,"w":"about"},{"t":25.734,"w":"rejection?"},{"t":28.237,"w":"Well,"},{"t":28.237,"w":"nobody"},{"t":28.237,"w":"likes"},{"t":28.237,"w":"rejection."},{"t":31.823,"w":"But"},{"t":31.823,"w":"I"},{"t":31.823,"w":"think"},{"t":31.823,"w":"as"},{"t":31.823,"w":"you"},{"t":31.823,"w":"get"},{"t":31.823,"w":"older,"},{"t":31.823,"w":"you"},{"t":31.823,"w":"get"},{"t":31.823,"w":"used"},{"t":31.823,"w":"to"},{"t":31.823,"w":"it."},{"t":35.661,"w":"And"},{"t":35.661,"w":"probably"},{"t":35.661,"w":"it's"},{"t":35.661,"w":"quit